course: dictionary
lesson: 15095
title: Rotted: when things break down
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Rotted is the past form of the verb rot. When something rots, it goes bad and slowly breaks down, often because of tiny germs, fungi, damp or age. «The apple rotted in the fruit bowl.» The apple did not go bad in one moment. Over days it turned soft and brown.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Words like damp, germs and slowly show what is happening. Then try your meaning in the sentence: «The apple went bad and broke down in the fruit bowl.» It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Rot can also be an adjective, but people usually say «rotten» instead. «The rotted wood creaked under my feet» means the same as «the rotten wood creaked». Rotten is the word you will hear most, so learn both.
fact: Rot means to go bad and break down slowly.
fact: «Rotted» is the past form of «rot», so it tells us something has already happened.
fact: Germs, fungi, damp and age can all make things rot.
fact: In science, bacteria and fungi break down dead plants and food into soil, called compost.
fact: Sugar can make teeth rot, which is why we brush them.
exercise: «The old fence rotted away in the rain.» What does rotted mean here? | Shone in the sun | Painted bright red | *Went bad and broke down slowly | Grew very quickly
exercise: «Fallen leaves rotted into rich brown soil.» What does this tell us? | *Leaves broke down slowly into soil | Leaves flew away in the wind | Leaves turned into stone | Leaves were swept into a bin
exercise: Dad says, «Throw out that rotten banana.» Which word means the same as rotten here? | Sweet | Yellow | *Decayed | Shiny
test: «Sugar can make your teeth rot if you forget to brush.» What does rot mean here? | Grow straight and strong | Shine brightly | Become very sweet | *Go bad and break down slowly
test: Which words in «The bread rotted in the damp box for a week» are clues to its meaning? | bread and box | rotted and the | *damp and for a week | in and the
exam: «Sam's old boots rotted in the damp garage.» What does rotted mean? | Were stolen | Shone brightly | *Went bad and broke down slowly | Grew taller
